1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:40,145 --> 00:00:41,062
This is it.

3
00:00:41,146 --> 00:00:42,272
What?

4
00:00:43,022 --> 00:00:44,023
Goodbye, Go Eun-sae.

5
00:00:44,607 --> 00:00:48,069
What do you mean?
Where are you telling me to go, alone?

6
00:00:51,030 --> 00:00:53,074
Jang Tae-ha!

7
00:00:53,158 --> 00:00:56,327
Jang Tae-ha!

8
00:00:56,411 --> 00:00:57,495
Jang Tae-ha.

9
00:00:57,579 --> 00:00:58,913
Jang Tae-ha!

10
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:11,885
What's with the strange dream?

11
00:01:14,012 --> 00:01:15,180
Actually, no.

12
00:01:15,263 --> 00:01:16,514
What about our marriage?

13
00:01:17,098 --> 00:01:18,391
Is that not happening?

14
00:01:22,937 --> 00:01:24,355
I guess it isn't that strange,

15
00:01:24,856 --> 00:01:26,691
since he doesn't even like me.

16
00:01:35,241 --> 00:01:39,120
Now that her memory has returned,
this whole act is over.

17
00:01:39,204 --> 00:01:42,123
Pretending to be her boyfriend,
being all close…

18
00:01:42,207 --> 00:01:44,209
Starting tomorrow, you can't do that.

19
00:02:13,321 --> 00:02:14,364
Are you okay?

20
00:02:15,114 --> 00:02:17,367
Don't act as if you care.

21
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:19,410
I know now that you don't.

22
00:02:21,955 --> 00:02:23,122
So you remember all of it?

23
00:02:25,041 --> 00:02:29,128
What kind of person Jang Tae-ha really is.

24
00:02:29,212 --> 00:02:31,130
I know everything now.

25
00:02:33,424 --> 00:02:34,425
Yes.

26
00:02:35,635 --> 00:02:37,011
So what will you do now?

27
00:02:37,804 --> 00:02:41,224
Now that everything's out in the open,
are you going to be honest?

28
00:02:41,808 --> 00:02:43,434
I know you must be confused.

29
00:02:43,518 --> 00:02:45,853
I'm sorry if our time together
was unpleasant.

30
00:02:46,729 --> 00:02:50,608
It was the best I could do.
Pretending we dated to bring you here.

31
00:02:50,692 --> 00:02:52,235
I couldn't leave you alone.

32
00:02:54,112 --> 00:02:55,029
Why not?

33
00:02:55,613 --> 00:02:56,656
Because you pitied me?

34
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:02,537
I may have lost my memory,
but I never asked for sympathy.

35
00:03:06,374 --> 00:03:07,917
Why didn't you just abandon me?

36
00:03:10,295 --> 00:03:11,796
As you now know,

37
00:03:12,588 --> 00:03:13,631
you have to leave.

38
00:03:16,634 --> 00:03:18,094
I found a place for you to go.

39
00:03:18,678 --> 00:03:22,765
You can leave next week. Until then,
stay here even if it's uncomfortable.

40
00:03:26,477 --> 00:03:27,478
Sorry for everything.

41
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:38,072
So people really do change overnight.

42
00:03:38,156 --> 00:03:39,991
I've just gone back to my old self.

43
00:03:48,791 --> 00:03:53,338
I really can't believe any of this,
so I'll ask you one last time.

44
00:03:54,464 --> 00:03:57,967
So you're saying
that everything you said and did for me

45
00:03:58,468 --> 00:03:59,677
was all fake?

46
00:04:01,888 --> 00:04:02,889
Yes.

47
00:04:04,098 --> 00:04:05,391
That it was all an act?

48
00:04:07,185 --> 00:04:08,019
Yes.

49
00:04:13,691 --> 00:04:14,525
Go Eun-sae.

50
00:04:19,405 --> 00:04:20,656
Why did you have to…

51
00:04:21,157 --> 00:04:22,492
Get a grip, Go Eun-sae!

52
00:04:28,039 --> 00:04:29,540
This isn't the time to get angry.

53
00:04:30,541 --> 00:04:31,876
It's time for you to leave.

54
00:04:39,384 --> 00:04:41,886
Stay here. I'll go buy some ointment.

55
00:05:01,364 --> 00:05:05,368
JUNGANG PHARMACY

56
00:05:17,672 --> 00:05:18,506
Go Eun-sae.

57
00:05:35,690 --> 00:05:37,150
Go Eun-sae!

58
00:05:39,944 --> 00:05:41,362
Go Eun-sae!

59
00:05:50,037 --> 00:05:52,290
If she remembered it all,
she should've been terrified.

60
00:05:52,373 --> 00:05:53,833
Where on earth did she go?

61
00:05:53,916 --> 00:05:56,961
You don't think she went
to the Seoul Prosecutor's Office, do you?

62
00:05:58,379 --> 00:06:01,424
Seoul is Baek Sang-gil's turf,
so she could be in real danger.

63
00:06:02,008 --> 00:06:03,259
And she left her phone.

64
00:06:03,843 --> 00:06:07,221
The fastest way to find her would be
to check the cameras from here to town.

65
00:06:07,305 --> 00:06:09,891
We'd need to report her missing,
but her identity is…

66
00:06:09,974 --> 00:06:12,310
Hey, don't worry about that.

67
00:06:12,393 --> 00:06:16,772
I've been drinking buddies with
the local police chief for a decade.

68
00:06:24,697 --> 00:06:26,073
Is there a party going on?

69
00:06:26,157 --> 00:06:27,909
Why are you all swarming out?

70
00:06:27,992 --> 00:06:29,619
Where's our girl, Eun-sae?

71
00:06:30,286 --> 00:06:31,579
Did you happen to see her?

72
00:06:32,622 --> 00:06:34,457
What are you talking about?

73
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:37,335
-We made it over here to comfort her.
-Comfort her?

74
00:06:38,211 --> 00:06:41,339
There's no such thing as secrets
in a teeny village like this.

75
00:06:41,422 --> 00:06:44,717
I heard she drank heaps
at the pub yesterday

76
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:48,679
because someone left her
completely torn up inside.

77
00:06:49,764 --> 00:06:50,598
Sorry?

78
00:06:51,807 --> 00:06:55,144
Fine! I'll say a few words as your elder.

79
00:06:55,228 --> 00:06:56,479
You, Tae-ha!

80
00:06:56,562 --> 00:06:57,855
You shouldn't do that.

81
00:06:57,939 --> 00:07:01,609
A woman's heart is fragile, easily broken
with a spoonful of cheap sympathy.

82
00:07:01,692 --> 00:07:05,321
You'd lost feelings a long while ago,
but you still held her hand everywhere.

83
00:07:05,404 --> 00:07:09,283
Treated her like a princess!
That's deceit! Deceit is what that is!

84
00:07:09,367 --> 00:07:10,368
That's right.

85
00:07:10,451 --> 00:07:14,288
What are you going to say next?
That Muhammed Ali got beaten up?

86
00:07:14,372 --> 00:07:17,917
What did he do to hear all this
cheap sympathy and deceit nonsense?

87
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,502
-What?
-Hold up.

88
00:07:19,585 --> 00:07:21,254
What are you all talking about?

89
00:07:23,631 --> 00:07:24,924
What are you talking about?

90
00:07:25,007 --> 00:07:26,926
Wait, so it's not like that?

91
00:07:27,009 --> 00:07:28,135
I guess not.

92
00:07:28,636 --> 00:07:29,929
-Well…
-Well, you see…

93
00:07:30,012 --> 00:07:32,515
We thought it was like that,
so that's what we told her.

94
00:07:32,598 --> 00:07:34,767
We didn't want Eun-sae to end up
being the fool.

95
00:07:34,850 --> 00:07:36,686
And what exactly did you tell her?

96
00:07:36,769 --> 00:07:38,604
-Well…
-We just…

97
00:07:39,105 --> 00:07:42,942
Tae-ha, you said
you weren't going to marry her.

98
00:07:43,025 --> 00:07:45,653
Yeah, that she had no memory
and no place to go,

99
00:07:45,736 --> 00:07:47,363
so you let her stay out of pity.

100
00:07:47,446 --> 00:07:49,365
That you don't see her that way.

101
00:07:49,865 --> 00:07:50,700
Sorry?

102
00:07:50,783 --> 00:07:52,785
Isn't that why you two fought yesterday?

103
00:07:52,868 --> 00:07:55,746
Yeong-sil from the pub said so.
That Eun-sae kept saying,

104
00:07:55,830 --> 00:07:59,709
"Why did you do all that
when you had no intention of marrying me?"

105
00:07:59,792 --> 00:08:00,876
What the…

106
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,128
Poor Eun-sae.

107
00:08:02,712 --> 00:08:05,423
So she wasn't drinking yesterday
because her memory returned?

108
00:08:11,512 --> 00:08:14,056
GUJIN-GUN OFFICE

109
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:15,182
Hello.

110
00:08:15,266 --> 00:08:17,310
Hello. How can I help you?

111
00:08:20,521 --> 00:08:23,232
I'm an unidentified person with no family.

112
00:08:24,567 --> 00:08:27,528
I have amnesia, so I don't know who I am.

113
00:08:27,612 --> 00:08:28,696
As for my identity…

114
00:08:31,198 --> 00:08:32,533
Goodness.

115
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:36,287
I couldn't find it because of this.

116
00:08:38,581 --> 00:08:42,501
I want to go to a government facility
that protects people like me.

117
00:08:43,002 --> 00:08:44,503
Darn it.

118
00:08:45,421 --> 00:08:49,634
So this was because you misunderstood,
as did all of you?

119
00:08:49,717 --> 00:08:53,346
All of this happened
because of a misunderstanding?

120
00:08:54,430 --> 00:08:56,349
-A misunderstanding?
-A mis…

121
00:08:56,432 --> 00:08:57,516
-Misunderstanding?
-How…

122
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,769
Hey, where are you going all of a sudden?

123
00:08:59,852 --> 00:09:02,104
-We need to check the CCTV footage now.
-Right.

124
00:09:16,661 --> 00:09:19,121
-There's Eun-sae, getting in a taxi.
-Yeah.

125
00:09:22,124 --> 00:09:23,250
Wait.

126
00:09:23,334 --> 00:09:25,503
-Isn't that Dal-su's taxi?
-Yeah!

127
00:09:25,586 --> 00:09:27,963
Go on, then. Hurry and call Dal-su.

128
00:09:28,047 --> 00:09:28,923
Yeah.

129
00:09:29,006 --> 00:09:30,049
Good heavens.

130
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:34,470
Oh boy.

131
00:09:34,553 --> 00:09:37,807
Tae-ha, I know it's important
to go and find your wife,

132
00:09:37,890 --> 00:09:40,267
but we still have
a lot of life left to live too!

133
00:09:40,351 --> 00:09:44,021
I still need to see Pil-seung get married!

134
00:09:54,615 --> 00:09:56,367
-Oh, Tae-ha!
-Goodness.

135
00:09:56,450 --> 00:09:58,119
-Sir!
-Goodness, Tae-ha!

136
00:10:02,206 --> 00:10:04,959
It's locked. Tae-ha, they're closed.

137
00:10:07,628 --> 00:10:10,506
-What's wrong?
-What is it? What?

138
00:10:11,132 --> 00:10:11,966
Tae-ha!

139
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:22,101
How'd he do that?

140
00:10:23,811 --> 00:10:27,773
If you know Ji-won,
you must know where she is.

141
00:10:28,649 --> 00:10:29,775
Where is she?

142
00:10:29,859 --> 00:10:31,235
I'll ask you first.

143
00:10:31,318 --> 00:10:33,863
What's your relationship with Ms. Ji-won?

144
00:10:36,949 --> 00:10:39,535
You didn't come here knowing everything?

145
00:10:39,618 --> 00:10:41,036
Please answer me first.

146
00:10:43,998 --> 00:10:45,624
Ji-won is my girlfriend.

147
00:10:47,001 --> 00:10:49,128
She's been missing for over a month.

148
00:10:50,463 --> 00:10:51,881
Do you have proof?

149
00:10:58,012 --> 00:10:59,638
Have a scroll through.

150
00:11:11,859 --> 00:11:15,738
If the photos aren't proof enough,
you can go to the Prosecutors' Office.

151
00:11:16,238 --> 00:11:17,531
-Prosecutors' Office?
-Yes.

152
00:11:17,615 --> 00:11:18,908
Prosecutor Go and I…

153
00:11:19,492 --> 00:11:23,579
Most of the guards, investigators,
and her fellow prosecutors knew about us.

154
00:11:27,041 --> 00:11:28,375
Prosecutor?

155
00:11:29,668 --> 00:11:31,128
Where is Ji-won?

156
00:11:34,423 --> 00:11:36,217
Gujin doesn't have any facilities.

157
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,636
They say you have to go
all the way to Dangjin.

158
00:11:39,136 --> 00:11:42,056
You'll stay at a temporary
homeless shelter for a few days

159
00:11:42,139 --> 00:11:44,099
before moving to a self-support center.

160
00:11:44,767 --> 00:11:47,978
My goodness, to lose your entire memory…

161
00:11:48,813 --> 00:11:52,441
Usually, people have at least someone
by their side in situations like these.

162
00:11:52,525 --> 00:11:53,984
Do you really not have anyone?

163
00:12:04,829 --> 00:12:06,121
Good grief!

164
00:12:07,331 --> 00:12:09,083
Damn it.

165
00:12:31,522 --> 00:12:34,066
What the heck was that for?
You can't just do that.

166
00:12:34,149 --> 00:12:36,068
You're asking for an accident, you know!

167
00:12:36,151 --> 00:12:37,403
I'm her husband.

168
00:12:45,828 --> 00:12:46,704
She's not alone.

169
00:12:47,371 --> 00:12:48,539
She has me by her side.

170
00:12:49,748 --> 00:12:50,583
What?

171
00:12:51,250 --> 00:12:52,543
And she has sisters.

172
00:12:53,252 --> 00:12:55,504
And a super obedient little brother.

173
00:12:55,588 --> 00:12:57,256
And a slightly older brother-in-law.

174
00:12:57,756 --> 00:13:00,551
And a friend who transcends age.

175
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:07,391
What's going on here?

176
00:13:09,059 --> 00:13:10,269
What is all this?

177
00:13:10,352 --> 00:13:13,606
That guy risked all our lives
to come here.

178
00:13:13,689 --> 00:13:16,191
He drove like it was a roller coaster.

179
00:13:16,275 --> 00:13:19,278
He even jumped over
the totem-pole-high county office gates.

180
00:13:19,361 --> 00:13:21,780
I thought he was going to take flight.

181
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:24,325
Why go to such lengths…

182
00:13:24,950 --> 00:13:26,827
Why do you think?

183
00:13:26,911 --> 00:13:29,496
He was worried
that he might lose his wife.

184
00:13:31,123 --> 00:13:32,333
That makes no sense.

185
00:13:32,917 --> 00:13:34,752
You told me to go.

186
00:13:35,336 --> 00:13:36,420
To leave.

187
00:13:39,506 --> 00:13:42,301
That was all our fault.

188
00:13:42,384 --> 00:13:44,553
We shouldn't have gotten involved.

189
00:13:44,637 --> 00:13:47,723
Turns out, we made you
misunderstand each other.

190
00:13:48,432 --> 00:13:49,808
Sorry.

191
00:13:54,021 --> 00:13:56,732
You weren't keeping me around
because you pitied me?

192
00:13:56,815 --> 00:13:57,775
That dog of yours.

193
00:13:58,484 --> 00:13:59,318
The dog.

194
00:13:59,902 --> 00:14:01,654
He was talking about the dog.

195
00:14:02,154 --> 00:14:03,614
You actually believed that?

196
00:14:04,573 --> 00:14:06,700
You said you didn't even see me that way.

197
00:14:06,784 --> 00:14:08,035
That was about Su-ji.

198
00:14:11,664 --> 00:14:14,458
I'm so nervous I can barely breathe,
even now.

199
00:14:15,417 --> 00:14:17,753
But you said you wouldn't marry me!

200
00:14:19,922 --> 00:14:21,799
Because everything you know about us

201
00:14:23,092 --> 00:14:24,426
is based on what I told you.

202
00:14:25,594 --> 00:14:26,971
When your memory comes back…

203
00:14:28,806 --> 00:14:30,891
If, when your memory returns…

204
00:14:32,518 --> 00:14:33,477
If you still

205
00:14:34,687 --> 00:14:35,980
feel that way about me…

206
00:14:38,190 --> 00:14:39,024
then…

207
00:14:40,693 --> 00:14:42,111
give me permission

208
00:14:43,654 --> 00:14:44,488
to marry you.

209
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:51,495
Are you serious?

210
00:14:54,748 --> 00:14:56,250
You don't hate me?

211
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:01,797
I can really stay?

212
00:15:04,550 --> 00:15:05,384
Go Eun-sae.

213
00:15:08,721 --> 00:15:09,555
Let's go

214
00:15:10,764 --> 00:15:11,598
home.

215
00:15:23,318 --> 00:15:28,407
It really felt like my world was ending.

216
00:15:29,116 --> 00:15:31,952
I was fearful of living without you.

217
00:15:32,453 --> 00:15:35,372
It felt so much like hell.

218
00:15:50,846 --> 00:15:53,140
Silly me. I'm tearing up.

219
00:15:54,141 --> 00:15:54,975
Right?

220
00:15:55,642 --> 00:15:58,479
Goodness me.
Why are you crying, young man?

221
00:15:59,104 --> 00:16:02,274
I cry whenever I see someone else cry.

222
00:16:17,164 --> 00:16:19,666
I bet their hands are all sweaty.

223
00:16:42,439 --> 00:16:43,357
What…

224
00:16:44,691 --> 00:16:46,485
What is all this?

225
00:16:57,996 --> 00:17:01,291
There's a reason we call him
Taffy Village's Choi Soo-jong.

226
00:17:06,505 --> 00:17:09,216
-Looks like her.
-Go on, then. Hurry and call Dal-su.

227
00:17:09,299 --> 00:17:10,884
-Yeah, okay.
-Goodness.

228
00:17:10,968 --> 00:17:13,679
It's a good thing
she got in Dal-su's taxi.

229
00:17:13,762 --> 00:17:15,681
-What is this?
-What's this?

230
00:17:16,431 --> 00:17:17,599
What is all this?

231
00:17:23,856 --> 00:17:25,315
Did you order these

232
00:17:25,399 --> 00:17:29,361
right after she said she liked
light pink roses yesterday morning?

233
00:17:38,787 --> 00:17:40,038
Deceit, my foot.

234
00:17:40,956 --> 00:17:42,499
Darn it.

235
00:17:43,041 --> 00:17:45,836
Let me call Dal-su…

236
00:17:48,338 --> 00:17:49,298
Is this because

237
00:17:49,798 --> 00:17:52,217
I said light pink roses are pretty?

238
00:17:55,512 --> 00:17:56,430
You like them.

239
00:18:00,434 --> 00:18:01,268
Honestly.

240
00:18:03,145 --> 00:18:04,396
You're impossible.

241
00:18:06,315 --> 00:18:08,942
I was just talking about a bouquet.

242
00:18:10,736 --> 00:18:13,280
There's no middle ground with this guy.

243
00:18:13,363 --> 00:18:15,824
As a boxer, he only won gold medals.
No silvers.

244
00:18:16,617 --> 00:18:18,827
Then, at school,
he was always last in his class.

245
00:18:20,204 --> 00:18:21,663
Come on, Coach.

246
00:18:22,497 --> 00:18:25,667
It's just so pretty.
Why don't you take a picture?

247
00:18:25,751 --> 00:18:27,628
Yes! It's so pretty.

248
00:18:27,711 --> 00:18:30,756
It's so pretty. You two should dress up
like a bride and groom.

249
00:18:30,839 --> 00:18:32,466
And take a picture here.

250
00:18:32,549 --> 00:18:33,508
Sounds good.

251
00:18:33,592 --> 00:18:34,968
Can we do that?

252
00:18:35,469 --> 00:18:36,970
I'd like to take a picture.

253
00:18:40,849 --> 00:18:41,850
Okay.

254
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:47,481
Okay, we'll take the picture now.
The bride and groom.

255
00:18:47,981 --> 00:18:50,150
Please hold hands.

256
00:18:51,902 --> 00:18:53,987
-What are you waiting for?
-How sweet!

257
00:18:54,071 --> 00:18:56,365
Okay, here goes. Three, two, one.

258
00:18:56,448 --> 00:18:58,200
-That's it.
-Perfect!

259
00:18:58,283 --> 00:18:59,243
How pretty.

260
00:18:59,326 --> 00:19:01,411
Okay, now face each other.

261
00:19:01,495 --> 00:19:03,997
-That's it!
-Look at each other.

262
00:19:04,081 --> 00:19:06,541
More. Face each other.

263
00:19:06,625 --> 00:19:11,421
Now, groom, hold out your hands.
Bride, place your hands on his.

264
00:19:11,505 --> 00:19:12,756
That's nice.

265
00:19:12,839 --> 00:19:14,466
Now look at the camera.

266
00:19:14,549 --> 00:19:16,843
Three, two, one!

267
00:19:23,684 --> 00:19:25,018
-You look lovely.
-Take care.

268
00:19:25,102 --> 00:19:27,145
-You look good.
-Take care, sir.

269
00:19:27,771 --> 00:19:28,605
Do well.

270
00:19:29,189 --> 00:19:30,065
Good night.

271
00:19:30,148 --> 00:19:31,942
-You too.
-Bye, So-wol.

272
00:19:32,025 --> 00:19:33,485
-See you.
-Good night.

273
00:19:33,568 --> 00:19:35,445
Congratulations? What is this, a wedding?

274
00:19:35,529 --> 00:19:36,571
Honestly.

275
00:19:36,655 --> 00:19:38,198
-Good night.
-One second.

276
00:19:38,782 --> 00:19:42,327
Now the misunderstanding
has all been cleared up,

277
00:19:42,411 --> 00:19:44,162
and this young man won't be around,

278
00:19:44,246 --> 00:19:46,748
which means tonight
is your first night alone.

279
00:19:46,832 --> 00:19:47,958
Goodness gracious!

280
00:19:48,542 --> 00:19:52,587
I hope you don't wake up the whole village
in the middle of the night.

281
00:19:52,671 --> 00:19:54,339
You're absolutely crazy.

282
00:19:54,423 --> 00:19:57,217
Tae-ha, what makes a man?
Confidence, okay?

283
00:19:57,301 --> 00:20:00,053
On a night like tonight,
a bed isn't a piece of furniture.

284
00:20:00,137 --> 00:20:01,388
It's a stage.

285
00:20:01,471 --> 00:20:03,348
In bed, a man must be confident!

286
00:20:03,432 --> 00:20:06,643
Please stop.
We'll take care of it ourselves.

287
00:20:06,727 --> 00:20:08,645
-Yourselves?
-They'll take care of it?

288
00:20:08,729 --> 00:20:09,771
Themselves?

289
00:20:10,272 --> 00:20:11,356
Please hurry home.

290
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:13,150
-Get home safe.
-Goodbye.

291
00:20:16,028 --> 00:20:17,988
I don't know why they're like that.

292
00:20:33,295 --> 00:20:34,546
Well…

293
00:20:34,629 --> 00:20:36,423
Yeah, well…

294
00:20:40,677 --> 00:20:41,553
Shall we…

295
00:20:41,636 --> 00:20:43,555
Shall we have a drink?

296
00:20:49,102 --> 00:20:52,022
Wow, you had something like this?

297
00:20:52,814 --> 00:20:55,025
You must be a total drinker,

298
00:20:55,108 --> 00:20:58,070
carrying something like this around
and drinking by yourself.

299
00:20:59,029 --> 00:20:59,905
You drank with me.

300
00:21:01,406 --> 00:21:03,742
I did? When?

301
00:21:04,743 --> 00:21:07,537
In Japan. Under the cherry blossoms.

302
00:21:09,456 --> 00:21:10,290
Cherry blossoms?

303
00:21:12,042 --> 00:21:14,544
This place is so beautiful.

304
00:21:19,132 --> 00:21:20,926
It must have been so romantic.

305
00:21:22,636 --> 00:21:24,763
I want my memory to return soon.

306
00:21:24,846 --> 00:21:28,809
It's so unfair that you're the only one
who remembers all of that good stuff.

307
00:21:38,026 --> 00:21:38,944
Perfect.

308
00:21:47,202 --> 00:21:48,870
By the way,

309
00:21:49,871 --> 00:21:52,874
what was it about what I said
that you misunderstood?

310
00:21:55,794 --> 00:21:56,795
What?

311
00:21:56,878 --> 00:22:01,550
The harsh things you said to me earlier
sounded so real.

312
00:22:02,134 --> 00:22:03,301
It scared me a little.

313
00:22:09,307 --> 00:22:12,060
The time we spent together
in Taffy Village…

314
00:22:13,687 --> 00:22:14,563
I thought

315
00:22:16,022 --> 00:22:17,524
you hated it all.

316
00:22:20,402 --> 00:22:21,528
There's no way.

317
00:22:27,951 --> 00:22:32,205
Someday, when time passes
and your memory returns,

318
00:22:33,707 --> 00:22:36,585
and even if the day comes
when you don't like me anymore,

319
00:22:38,462 --> 00:22:39,588
I hope our time together

320
00:22:40,589 --> 00:22:43,008
won't be a painful memory for you.

321
00:22:50,765 --> 00:22:52,976
You really like me, don't you?

322
00:22:53,477 --> 00:22:56,188
Worrying about things you don't need to.

323
00:22:57,772 --> 00:23:00,901
There's no way I'd ever not like you.

324
00:23:03,945 --> 00:23:07,407
But why do you like me so much?

325
00:23:08,658 --> 00:23:12,245
-You're p--
-Don't say it's because I'm pretty.

326
00:23:12,329 --> 00:23:13,455
That's so cliché.

327
00:23:15,874 --> 00:23:17,959
I was going to say
it's because you're polite.

328
00:23:20,837 --> 00:23:21,671
What?

329
00:23:22,422 --> 00:23:23,798
Say that again.

330
00:23:24,299 --> 00:23:26,468
You're actually quite polite,

331
00:23:27,010 --> 00:23:28,720
subtly taking care of Grandma.

332
00:23:29,304 --> 00:23:30,764
And up until a moment ago,

333
00:23:31,598 --> 00:23:33,808
you spoke formally to me.

334
00:23:37,854 --> 00:23:40,232
Seriously, stop joking around.

335
00:23:40,315 --> 00:23:43,026
Tell me why you really like me. Now.

336
00:23:43,109 --> 00:23:43,944
I don't know.

337
00:23:48,031 --> 00:23:50,450
Come on, you really have nothing to say?

338
00:23:50,534 --> 00:23:52,452
I really don't know. I just

339
00:23:53,078 --> 00:23:54,329
don't like other women.

340
00:24:00,085 --> 00:24:01,461
When I'm with you, I get…

341
00:24:03,588 --> 00:24:04,548
a little weird.

342
00:24:12,973 --> 00:24:14,307
You know what?

343
00:24:15,559 --> 00:24:16,851
I'm like that too.

344
00:24:19,104 --> 00:24:20,605
I get nervous, too,

345
00:24:21,189 --> 00:24:22,857
when I'm with you.

346
00:24:26,027 --> 00:24:27,487
I can barely breathe.

347
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:37,789
Now I like you more than Cha Eun-woo.

348
00:24:37,872 --> 00:24:42,127
And the password to my new email
is "Jang Tae-ha."

349
00:24:42,210 --> 00:24:44,963
The first face that comes to mind
when I wake up,

350
00:24:45,046 --> 00:24:49,467
and the last face that comes to mind
before I go to sleep, is Jang Tae-ha's.

351
00:24:56,808 --> 00:24:58,059
I like you.

352
00:25:03,189 --> 00:25:04,482
A lot.

353
00:26:39,369 --> 00:26:40,787
Gi-jun, what brings you here--

354
00:26:40,870 --> 00:26:42,497
What the hell are you up to?

355
00:26:43,581 --> 00:26:45,166
-What?
-I know everything.

356
00:26:45,250 --> 00:26:47,168
Who she really is, who you've been hiding.

357
00:26:49,546 --> 00:26:52,841
Anti-corruption Prosecutor Go Ji-won
from the Seoul Prosecutors' Office.

358
00:26:55,260 --> 00:26:56,594
Tell me.

359
00:26:57,679 --> 00:26:58,513
How did you know?

360
00:26:59,431 --> 00:27:01,141
I just met with Gwak Chi-hyeon.

361
00:27:01,725 --> 00:27:05,019
Go Eun-sae… I mean, Prosecutor Go Ji-won.
He's looking for her.

362
00:27:05,103 --> 00:27:08,273
How do you know about him?
How much did you tell him?

363
00:27:09,190 --> 00:27:11,568
-Did you tell him that she's here?
-Answer me first.

364
00:27:11,651 --> 00:27:14,320
What happened?
Do you know that this is a crime?

365
00:27:23,913 --> 00:27:25,540
Gi-jun, let's talk for a second.

366
00:27:29,794 --> 00:27:32,589
I need to meet Chairman Baek.

367
00:27:44,434 --> 00:27:48,021
So, you saved Go Eun-sae
when you were supposed to kill her,

368
00:27:48,813 --> 00:27:51,775
and you pretended to be her boyfriend
to keep her safe.

369
00:27:52,734 --> 00:27:55,904
And because she would only agree to flee
if she regained her memory,

370
00:27:55,987 --> 00:27:57,781
you were sincere about her treatment.

371
00:27:58,364 --> 00:27:59,199
Is that right?

372
00:28:03,328 --> 00:28:05,538
So they really, you know,

373
00:28:05,622 --> 00:28:10,293
make you… kill people and stuff?

374
00:28:12,670 --> 00:28:15,673
The man you met, Gwak Chi-hyeon,
is one of Baek Sang-gil's men.

375
00:28:16,466 --> 00:28:19,761
If he knows that she's alive,
he'll probably tell Baek Sang-gil.

376
00:28:25,391 --> 00:28:26,226
Now tell me.

377
00:28:27,852 --> 00:28:29,562
How much did you tell Gwak Chi-hyeon?

378
00:28:35,443 --> 00:28:36,611
Everything?

379
00:28:37,737 --> 00:28:38,571
Well…

380
00:28:41,449 --> 00:28:44,118
I don't even know why I did that.

381
00:28:47,914 --> 00:28:49,040
Where is Ji-won?

382
00:28:57,966 --> 00:28:59,551
I think I'm in the wrong place.

383
00:28:59,634 --> 00:29:00,593
Sorry?

384
00:29:01,302 --> 00:29:03,972
The Go Ji-won I know is not this person.

385
00:29:04,055 --> 00:29:06,099
What is this all of a sudden?

386
00:29:08,393 --> 00:29:11,479
This Go Ji-won… I mean, another Go Ji-won

387
00:29:12,188 --> 00:29:14,816
has caused a lot of harm
to a lot of people.

388
00:29:14,899 --> 00:29:16,860
So I was looking for her,

389
00:29:16,943 --> 00:29:19,529
but it seems they just share
the same name.

390
00:29:21,030 --> 00:29:23,199
Then how did you get my number?

391
00:29:25,285 --> 00:29:26,452
Well,

392
00:29:27,412 --> 00:29:31,708
I had someone look into
Go Ji-won's acquaintances,

393
00:29:31,791 --> 00:29:35,795
but I think the private investigator
made a mistake.

394
00:29:39,591 --> 00:29:43,720
Anyway, I don't know this person.
I apologize for the inconvenience.

395
00:29:43,803 --> 00:29:45,430
Wait. Excuse me?

396
00:29:49,058 --> 00:29:52,937
You and I were never that close,

397
00:29:53,021 --> 00:29:57,650
and we were polar opposites,
the top student and the bottom student.

398
00:29:57,734 --> 00:30:00,194
But I know you're not a bad guy.

399
00:30:00,778 --> 00:30:03,948
I wanted to hear you out first

400
00:30:04,032 --> 00:30:07,452
before deciding whether to hand her over
to Gwak Chi-hyeon or call the cops.

401
00:30:08,453 --> 00:30:09,787
Right, thanks.

402
00:30:10,455 --> 00:30:12,081
I really mean it. Thanks, Gi-jun.

403
00:30:13,833 --> 00:30:14,876
No problem.

404
00:30:15,752 --> 00:30:17,086
But

405
00:30:18,296 --> 00:30:21,633
if Go Eun-sae never gets her memory back,

406
00:30:22,425 --> 00:30:23,676
what are you going to do?

407
00:30:27,472 --> 00:30:29,223
I'll have to force her to leave.

408
00:30:29,974 --> 00:30:31,142
But if I do that,

409
00:30:32,352 --> 00:30:34,062
Go Eun-sae will be devastated.

410
00:30:35,939 --> 00:30:37,065
I actually meant to ask.

411
00:30:37,565 --> 00:30:40,735
Is there really no way
to get her memory back faster?

412
00:30:42,737 --> 00:30:45,365
The treatment's already brought back
some of her memory.

413
00:30:45,448 --> 00:30:47,492
Like her remembering Gwak Chi-hyeon.

414
00:30:48,576 --> 00:30:49,535
From now on,

415
00:30:49,619 --> 00:30:55,458
you need to help her see, feel,
and experience things from her past

416
00:30:56,042 --> 00:30:58,169
to trigger any memories related to them.

417
00:31:02,799 --> 00:31:05,927
I've been dying to ask you.

418
00:31:06,010 --> 00:31:09,931
What's with all these flowers?

419
00:31:10,932 --> 00:31:11,766
What?

420
00:31:14,644 --> 00:31:15,770
Oh, these?

421
00:31:16,854 --> 00:31:19,941
Go Eun-sae said roses are pretty.

422
00:31:21,275 --> 00:31:22,443
And women,

423
00:31:23,403 --> 00:31:25,196
they like this sort of thing?

424
00:31:26,698 --> 00:31:27,824
What?

425
00:31:30,952 --> 00:31:31,869
Never mind.

426
00:31:32,787 --> 00:31:33,871
I'm going.

427
00:31:34,372 --> 00:31:35,206
Okay.

428
00:31:38,001 --> 00:31:39,669
Can I take one of these?

429
00:31:40,169 --> 00:31:42,588
Yeah, sure. You can take a lot.

430
00:31:43,089 --> 00:31:45,675
These roses are unique.

431
00:32:02,567 --> 00:32:03,860
That bastard.

432
00:32:04,819 --> 00:32:06,237
He's so damn cool.

433
00:32:07,739 --> 00:32:09,198
-Trouble?
-Yes.

434
00:32:09,699 --> 00:32:13,828
I keep thinking that Prosecutor Go
might have gotten into some trouble.

435
00:32:13,911 --> 00:32:16,581
If today was about sending someone
to test the waters,

436
00:32:16,664 --> 00:32:19,167
he should have asked me something.

437
00:32:19,250 --> 00:32:21,919
But he didn't ask me anything significant.

438
00:32:22,545 --> 00:32:24,589
What are the chances
of a true coincidence?

439
00:32:24,672 --> 00:32:29,218
No, he definitely reacted
to the photos of Prosecutor Go.

440
00:32:33,181 --> 00:32:34,724
She got into some trouble…

441
00:32:34,807 --> 00:32:39,645
Maybe she got seriously injured
or was kidnapped by someone.

442
00:32:41,397 --> 00:32:43,483
That's why I came to see you, sir.

443
00:32:45,359 --> 00:32:49,155
Please trace the phone number
of the man I met today.

444
00:32:49,822 --> 00:32:52,658
I'm sure he is somehow connected
to Prosecutor Go.

445
00:32:58,664 --> 00:33:01,459
Come on.

446
00:33:02,418 --> 00:33:04,128
On such an important night,

447
00:33:04,212 --> 00:33:08,341
why did I have to go and get wasted
and fall asleep?

448
00:33:08,424 --> 00:33:10,802
Stupid.

449
00:33:24,440 --> 00:33:25,274
That's right.

450
00:33:25,358 --> 00:33:26,567
Last night.

451
00:33:27,068 --> 00:33:29,570
I remember
the atmosphere was really tense.

452
00:33:29,654 --> 00:33:31,697
Why would the two of them be like that?

453
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:38,704
Did they fight over me?

454
00:33:40,623 --> 00:33:41,624
What am I going to do?

455
00:33:41,707 --> 00:33:42,834
You're up?

456
00:33:43,960 --> 00:33:45,253
Jang Tae-ha.

457
00:33:45,336 --> 00:33:47,296
Doctor An came by last night, didn't he?

458
00:33:48,965 --> 00:33:49,966
Yes.

459
00:33:50,842 --> 00:33:52,093
How did you know?

460
00:33:52,176 --> 00:33:54,762
I thought I saw him
when I briefly woke up.

461
00:33:58,349 --> 00:34:00,518
Don't worry too much.

462
00:34:00,601 --> 00:34:02,770
I'll give him a serious talking-to.

463
00:34:06,607 --> 00:34:08,151
WE UNDERSTAND YOUR FEELINGS

464
00:34:08,234 --> 00:34:09,986
Lean back comfortably for a bit.

465
00:34:11,696 --> 00:34:14,157
I'm not comfortable
because of you, Doctor.

466
00:34:14,740 --> 00:34:15,575
Sorry?

467
00:34:15,658 --> 00:34:19,537
I think I should say this
before we start the treatment.

468
00:34:19,620 --> 00:34:22,248
Since you came all the way
to our home last night.

469
00:34:23,416 --> 00:34:25,793
I know we've gotten a lot closer recently.

470
00:34:25,877 --> 00:34:29,463
I got drunk, and you carried me home.

471
00:34:29,547 --> 00:34:31,591
I must have made a scene.

472
00:34:32,216 --> 00:34:33,467
But that wasn't a sign

473
00:34:33,551 --> 00:34:37,763
that you could cross the line.

474
00:34:39,432 --> 00:34:41,684
I'm in a common-law marriage.

475
00:34:42,643 --> 00:34:45,897
We haven't had a wedding yet,
but we're practically married.

476
00:34:45,980 --> 00:34:47,773
And I really,

477
00:34:48,274 --> 00:34:50,151
really like Jang Tae-ha.

478
00:34:50,651 --> 00:34:52,403
So I'm sorry,

479
00:34:52,486 --> 00:34:55,448
but I hope we can remain

480
00:34:56,032 --> 00:34:59,660
as a doctor and a patient.

481
00:35:00,620 --> 00:35:03,206
What is this nonsense?
Did you drink again?

482
00:35:03,289 --> 00:35:04,123
What?

483
00:35:04,207 --> 00:35:05,374
Wow, this is…

484
00:35:05,458 --> 00:35:07,418
This is bad. My goodness.

485
00:35:07,919 --> 00:35:09,212
Where do I even start? Okay.

486
00:35:09,295 --> 00:35:11,923
I'm sorry, but Ms. Go Eun-sae,

487
00:35:12,006 --> 00:35:13,507
you're not my type.

488
00:35:14,675 --> 00:35:16,761
I like women who look pure and innocent

489
00:35:16,844 --> 00:35:19,430
and have eyes
that point to twenty past eight.

490
00:35:19,513 --> 00:35:22,058
But looking at you now,

491
00:35:22,141 --> 00:35:24,977
your eyes are more… thirteen past nine.

492
00:35:25,061 --> 00:35:29,232
And what's more,
I don't like women who are too tall.

493
00:35:29,982 --> 00:35:31,400
I have a bad neck, so…

494
00:35:31,484 --> 00:35:34,278
Then why did you suddenly come to see
Jang Tae-ha last night

495
00:35:34,362 --> 00:35:36,822
and look up at him
like you were picking a fight?

496
00:35:36,906 --> 00:35:38,699
Hey, I did not look up at him!

497
00:35:38,783 --> 00:35:40,993
We were totally eye to eye!

498
00:35:41,077 --> 00:35:43,704
You were looking up at him like this!

499
00:35:43,788 --> 00:35:45,373
Ms. Eun-sae, sit down, okay?

500
00:35:45,456 --> 00:35:47,375
-Wait a second.
-You're here for treatment.

501
00:35:52,255 --> 00:35:53,422
I'm done. Let's go.

502
00:35:55,091 --> 00:35:56,592
Have a safe trip home.

503
00:36:00,346 --> 00:36:02,223
I like women who look pure and innocent

504
00:36:02,306 --> 00:36:04,809
and have eyes
that point to twenty past eight.

505
00:36:12,191 --> 00:36:13,442
Just put something down.

506
00:36:14,318 --> 00:36:15,653
-Just wait.
-Oh, come on!

507
00:36:15,736 --> 00:36:17,071
-Seriously?
-Did you see that?

508
00:36:17,154 --> 00:36:18,364
-How the heck?
-Here goes!

509
00:36:18,864 --> 00:36:20,658
What even is this?

510
00:36:20,741 --> 00:36:22,827
A double sweep. Cough up two cards each.

511
00:36:22,910 --> 00:36:24,620
Come on!

512
00:36:24,704 --> 00:36:27,331
All the top cards are going to you today.

513
00:36:27,415 --> 00:36:30,626
And you got all the double junk cards.
It's your lucky day.

514
00:36:30,710 --> 00:36:32,253
Tell me about it.

515
00:36:32,336 --> 00:36:35,631
I wonder what good thing
is going to happen to me…

516
00:36:35,715 --> 00:36:37,425
Should I buy a lottery ticket?

517
00:36:38,134 --> 00:36:39,218
I avoided the penalty.

518
00:36:39,302 --> 00:36:41,178
Isn't that Pil-seung?

519
00:36:41,887 --> 00:36:42,847
Oh my.

520
00:36:42,930 --> 00:36:47,059
He's marching over here like Lee Jung-jae
in The Face Reader.

521
00:37:00,531 --> 00:37:01,824
Let's go. Come on.

522
00:37:01,907 --> 00:37:02,825
Wait, Mom.

523
00:37:02,908 --> 00:37:03,993
Oh, shut it.

524
00:37:04,076 --> 00:37:05,494
Mom, please.

525
00:37:05,578 --> 00:37:08,372
Why does it have to be fist fights?

526
00:37:08,456 --> 00:37:12,668
I raised you for 17 years, making sure
you never got a single scratch.

527
00:37:12,752 --> 00:37:15,755
And now you want me
to watch some scary punks

528
00:37:15,838 --> 00:37:16,839
whack you on the head?

529
00:37:16,922 --> 00:37:19,133
I won't get whacked. I'll hit them harder.

530
00:37:21,218 --> 00:37:25,014
All right. Let's say you do well
and even win a medal.

531
00:37:25,931 --> 00:37:29,643
What will you do after you retire?
Who'd hire a guy who fought for a living?

532
00:37:29,727 --> 00:37:33,856
People will just call you empty-headed
wherever you go.

533
00:37:34,357 --> 00:37:36,609
-What if I fill my head?
-What's this now?

534
00:37:36,692 --> 00:37:40,363
If I'm good at boxing and get smart,
no one will be able to say that.

535
00:37:40,446 --> 00:37:41,989
You're going to study?

536
00:37:42,073 --> 00:37:44,575
You're the last in your whole school.

537
00:37:44,658 --> 00:37:47,161
If I do well on the next mock exam,
let me box.

538
00:37:47,244 --> 00:37:48,871
Is that a deal or not?

539
00:37:51,332 --> 00:37:52,249
What's wrong?

540
00:37:54,377 --> 00:37:55,628
Why are you… A report card?

541
00:37:56,212 --> 00:37:58,005
-A report card?
-It's Pil-seung's.

542
00:37:58,089 --> 00:37:59,173
What place…

543
00:37:59,256 --> 00:38:01,384
Fifth… in the whole school.

544
00:38:01,467 --> 00:38:02,510
Fifth in your school?

545
00:38:02,593 --> 00:38:04,428
Pil-seung! Goodness, Hui-ja!

546
00:38:04,512 --> 00:38:08,182
There's no doubt about it.
It's five, just like five top cards!

547
00:38:08,265 --> 00:38:09,100
Five!

548
00:38:14,814 --> 00:38:16,732
Fine, you can box.

549
00:38:18,984 --> 00:38:22,613
You must have really wanted this
if you went from last to fifth place.

550
00:38:22,696 --> 00:38:24,698
I'm going to the nationals
in two days' time.

551
00:38:27,243 --> 00:38:28,702
But

552
00:38:28,786 --> 00:38:32,248
can you go there just like that?

553
00:38:32,331 --> 00:38:33,582
I applied three months ago.

554
00:38:34,542 --> 00:38:36,168
I planned on competing anyway.

555
00:38:36,669 --> 00:38:40,423
But you haven't been able to train
because you've been studying.

556
00:38:40,506 --> 00:38:42,925
No. I haven't taken
a single day off from training.

557
00:39:04,321 --> 00:39:05,781
Other than eating and pooping,

558
00:39:05,865 --> 00:39:08,492
I studied and trained
as if my life depended on it.

559
00:39:09,034 --> 00:39:10,161
Now that you know,

560
00:39:10,244 --> 00:39:12,288
I thought I'd be up front
and ask permission.

561
00:39:17,376 --> 00:39:18,210
Okay.

562
00:39:18,711 --> 00:39:21,422
A promise is a promise.
You can compete in that thingy.

563
00:39:21,505 --> 00:39:22,590
You mean that?

564
00:39:23,174 --> 00:39:24,133
But

565
00:39:25,301 --> 00:39:26,135
I'm not going.

566
00:39:27,511 --> 00:39:32,183
I can't bear to see someone
whacking you in the head.

567
00:39:33,976 --> 00:39:35,895
Don't make me sit through that too.

568
00:39:38,606 --> 00:39:39,732
Please look after him.

569
00:39:41,150 --> 00:39:42,276
Mrs. Pang…

570
00:39:48,657 --> 00:39:51,744
I heard that Prosecutor Go Ji-won is alive

571
00:39:53,037 --> 00:39:55,831
and that she's holding a knife
to our throats.

572
00:39:57,124 --> 00:39:58,626
How did you find out about that?

573
00:39:58,709 --> 00:40:01,003
Did you really think
that when my previous aide

574
00:40:01,086 --> 00:40:06,133
made a mess and still survived you,
I wouldn't have him tailed?

575
00:40:07,801 --> 00:40:08,677
Well, well.

576
00:40:08,761 --> 00:40:10,804
I didn't know
our mayor was capable of that.

577
00:40:11,472 --> 00:40:14,600
I wonder why someone in silk robes
would dirty themselves with mud.

578
00:40:14,683 --> 00:40:16,644
Then you should have cleaned up properly!

579
00:40:19,730 --> 00:40:22,733
You couldn't even handle
a rookie nobody prosecutor

580
00:40:22,816 --> 00:40:24,026
and left crumbs behind?

581
00:40:24,902 --> 00:40:25,819
Makes me uneasy.

582
00:40:27,821 --> 00:40:31,158
The party is all in, building me up
as a presidential candidate.

583
00:40:32,117 --> 00:40:33,118
Momentum's good.

584
00:40:33,202 --> 00:40:36,288
I'm close to moving into the house
adorned with the rose of Sharon.

585
00:40:36,872 --> 00:40:37,706
Don't sully it.

586
00:40:37,790 --> 00:40:41,460
I buried 11 corpses
under the roots of that rose of Sharon.

587
00:40:44,088 --> 00:40:48,384
If I, Baek Sang-gil, were to become
a mad dog and dig up that land…

588
00:40:51,178 --> 00:40:53,222
they'd all come out into the open.

589
00:40:54,265 --> 00:40:55,766
Could you handle that?

590
00:40:59,353 --> 00:41:00,354
So,

591
00:41:00,437 --> 00:41:02,898
let's not waste time
barking at each other.

592
00:41:02,982 --> 00:41:06,569
I'm looking for her,
and I won't let anything go wrong.

593
00:41:13,659 --> 00:41:15,786
-I'll be going now, Coach.
-Yeah, good work.

594
00:41:15,869 --> 00:41:17,663
-Goodbye.
-Bye.

595
00:41:17,746 --> 00:41:19,373
-Get home safe.
-You got it!

596
00:41:21,542 --> 00:41:24,253
Pil-seung is awesome.

597
00:41:24,336 --> 00:41:26,422
So youthful spirit wins everything.

598
00:41:27,256 --> 00:41:28,340
Oh, right!

599
00:41:28,424 --> 00:41:30,968
I want to go cheer for Pil-seung
at his match.

600
00:41:31,051 --> 00:41:32,636
It's too dangerous to leave…

601
00:41:33,512 --> 00:41:39,476
You need to help her see, feel,
and experience things from her past.

602
00:41:40,644 --> 00:41:42,438
Okay, let's go together.

603
00:41:43,022 --> 00:41:45,024
Really? Yay!

604
00:41:48,235 --> 00:41:50,362
That one. Is that yours?

605
00:41:51,947 --> 00:41:54,658
Yeah, it's a medal I got back
thanks to my first love.

606
00:41:56,619 --> 00:41:59,288
Why are you bringing up
your first love right now?

607
00:42:09,632 --> 00:42:11,759
Do you want to hit this if you're angry?

608
00:42:15,304 --> 00:42:18,682
Mention your first love again and see
what happens. I'm the jealous type.

609
00:42:19,808 --> 00:42:23,395
By the way, I was in your room yesterday.
It's so drafty in there.

610
00:42:24,605 --> 00:42:25,439
No, it's not.

611
00:42:25,939 --> 00:42:27,066
Yes, it is.

612
00:42:27,733 --> 00:42:31,403
Why don't you sleep in my room from now on
so you don't catch a cold?

613
00:42:33,197 --> 00:42:35,032
Is that all you think about?

614
00:42:35,532 --> 00:42:39,119
Yes, of course.
I only think about you all day long.

615
00:42:39,203 --> 00:42:40,996
We're not sharing a bed.

616
00:42:42,456 --> 00:42:44,625
And why not?

617
00:42:44,708 --> 00:42:46,960
I told you. You make me nervous.

618
00:42:47,461 --> 00:42:48,921
I need to prepare myself.

619
00:42:55,010 --> 00:42:56,095
Fine.

620
00:42:56,178 --> 00:43:00,516
Then I'll give you a few days
to prepare yourself.

621
00:43:00,599 --> 00:43:02,893
I think I've gained some weight recently,

622
00:43:02,976 --> 00:43:04,478
so I should get back in shape.

623
00:43:05,187 --> 00:43:06,021
You haven't.

624
00:43:06,814 --> 00:43:07,815
You're pretty.

625
00:43:09,191 --> 00:43:10,693
So you know the right answer.

626
00:43:10,776 --> 00:43:12,945
Quite a master at flirting, aren't you?

627
00:43:13,612 --> 00:43:15,739
Be honest.
You've dated a lot, haven't you?

628
00:43:15,823 --> 00:43:17,866
-I haven't.
-As if.

629
00:43:17,950 --> 00:43:20,953
I'll forgive you if you tell me now.
But you have to tell me now.

630
00:43:21,036 --> 00:43:22,162
Be honest.

631
00:43:37,261 --> 00:43:40,264
THE 107TH NATIONAL SPORTS FESTIVAL
HIGH SCHOOL BOXING MATCH

632
00:43:40,347 --> 00:43:42,349
We need to get the confetti ready.

633
00:43:47,771 --> 00:43:48,605
BOXING ARENA

634
00:43:55,863 --> 00:43:56,822
Ladies!

635
00:43:57,406 --> 00:43:59,867
-There you are.
-Over here.

636
00:43:59,950 --> 00:44:02,786
-We're coming.
-What is all this?

637
00:44:02,870 --> 00:44:04,246
This is amazing!

638
00:44:04,329 --> 00:44:08,083
We're Pil-seung's aunties
who even changed his diapers.

639
00:44:08,167 --> 00:44:10,711
-This is the least we can do.
-Yeah.

640
00:44:10,794 --> 00:44:13,630
In case folks look down on him
for being from the country.

641
00:44:13,714 --> 00:44:15,841
Who would look down on him
after seeing this?

642
00:44:15,924 --> 00:44:18,343
We're like some kind of gang right now.

643
00:44:18,427 --> 00:44:19,928
Oh, come on.

644
00:44:21,013 --> 00:44:23,599
Pil-seung is coming out.
I think it's starting.

645
00:44:23,682 --> 00:44:24,808
There! Pil-seung!

646
00:44:24,892 --> 00:44:25,893
The pride of Gujin!

647
00:44:25,976 --> 00:44:28,771
-Kim Pil-seung, go get them!
-You've got this!

648
00:44:28,854 --> 00:44:30,314
Go, Pil-seung!

649
00:44:31,523 --> 00:44:33,108
-It's starting.
-Tae-ha.

650
00:44:33,192 --> 00:44:34,526
Look at me. Are you nervous?

651
00:44:35,110 --> 00:44:36,361
Do your best.

652
00:44:41,784 --> 00:44:43,702
-Pil-seung has…
-Taffy fists!

653
00:44:55,631 --> 00:44:57,174
KO! Red corner wins by KO!

654
00:44:59,092 --> 00:45:00,552
ROUND OF 16

655
00:45:01,470 --> 00:45:06,809
OH SEUNG-HYEON VS KIM PIL-SEUNG

656
00:45:07,643 --> 00:45:09,061
QUARTERFINALS

657
00:45:09,895 --> 00:45:16,902
JUNG GANG-SAN VS KIM PIL-SEUNG

658
00:45:19,696 --> 00:45:20,989
SEMIFINALS

659
00:45:21,073 --> 00:45:25,536
JOO YEONG-MIN VS KIM PIL-SEUNG

660
00:45:29,915 --> 00:45:31,750
That's it! Back away now.

661
00:45:38,173 --> 00:45:39,216
FINAL

662
00:45:39,299 --> 00:45:42,094
GUJIN HIGH, KIM PIL-SEUNG
VS YONGDEOK HIGH, CHOI WON-UK

663
00:45:42,177 --> 00:45:45,138
The high school boxing final
will begin shortly.

664
00:45:47,432 --> 00:45:49,560
Pil-seung, this is the last match.

665
00:45:50,269 --> 00:45:51,103
You've done great.

666
00:45:51,812 --> 00:45:53,063
Don't get nervous

667
00:45:53,146 --> 00:45:55,440
and stay focused until the end, okay?

668
00:45:58,735 --> 00:45:59,736
Let's go!

669
00:46:07,744 --> 00:46:08,871
Swing your arms!

670
00:46:09,705 --> 00:46:11,123
More!

671
00:46:16,211 --> 00:46:17,170
That's it! Again!

672
00:46:28,473 --> 00:46:29,850
Get off him.

673
00:46:41,028 --> 00:46:42,112
Damn it!

674
00:46:42,779 --> 00:46:44,239
Excuse me. Please move aside!

675
00:46:47,200 --> 00:46:48,035
Hold on.

676
00:46:51,622 --> 00:46:54,207
Pil-seung, are you okay?

677
00:46:56,251 --> 00:46:58,045
Oh no, what do we do?

678
00:46:59,963 --> 00:47:02,507
Don't you even maintain
the facilities here?

679
00:47:03,091 --> 00:47:06,678
Oh dear. This isn't the kind of bleeding
that will stop anytime soon.

680
00:47:07,429 --> 00:47:10,557
It looks pretty serious,
so we should end the match now.

681
00:47:10,641 --> 00:47:13,101
Let's rule it a loss by decision
for Kim Pil-seung.

682
00:47:13,185 --> 00:47:14,186
No, you can't!

683
00:47:14,269 --> 00:47:15,270
You can't do that.

684
00:47:15,354 --> 00:47:16,980
You should reschedule the match!

685
00:47:17,064 --> 00:47:18,231
According to the rules,

686
00:47:18,315 --> 00:47:22,152
it's up to me, the TD, to decide
whether to reschedule or rule it a loss.

687
00:47:22,736 --> 00:47:24,696
So reschedule the match.

688
00:47:24,780 --> 00:47:26,782
We can do it some other day!

689
00:47:26,865 --> 00:47:29,201
Come on, you know how it is.

690
00:47:29,284 --> 00:47:33,246
Don't you know how complicated it is
to reschedule a match?

691
00:47:33,330 --> 00:47:35,582
Then you'd be happy for us
to take legal action?

692
00:47:36,708 --> 00:47:39,378
-Sorry?
-It's in Article 2 of the Civil Act.

693
00:47:39,461 --> 00:47:41,171
The organizers of a sports event

694
00:47:41,254 --> 00:47:44,800
have a duty, in good faith,
to protect athletes during a competition.

695
00:47:44,883 --> 00:47:48,637
In this case, not only was the athlete
injured due to the organizers' negligence,

696
00:47:48,720 --> 00:47:51,014
he now risks losing his chance at gold.

697
00:47:51,098 --> 00:47:51,974
You tell them!

698
00:47:52,057 --> 00:47:54,101
If this isn't resolved properly,

699
00:47:54,184 --> 00:47:58,563
we will file a lawsuit for breach of duty
regarding injury and medical treatment.

700
00:47:58,647 --> 00:48:00,482
-That's right!
-Yes, a lawsuit!

701
00:48:05,946 --> 00:48:08,991
Then please wait
in the waiting room for now.

702
00:48:09,741 --> 00:48:12,077
-What the heck?
-What are you playing at?

703
00:48:12,160 --> 00:48:14,079
How long do you expect us to wait?

704
00:48:14,162 --> 00:48:15,288
Is he okay?

705
00:48:15,372 --> 00:48:16,748
Pil-seung, are you okay?

706
00:48:16,832 --> 00:48:18,542
-How is it?
-Can I take a look?

707
00:48:18,625 --> 00:48:20,043
He's bleeding too much.

708
00:48:20,127 --> 00:48:23,088
-Oh dear. What if it scars?
-This is so upsetting.

709
00:48:26,925 --> 00:48:28,510
By the way,

710
00:48:28,593 --> 00:48:31,263
how did you know so much
about the law earlier?

711
00:48:31,346 --> 00:48:32,597
Yeah, exactly.

712
00:48:32,681 --> 00:48:35,183
-You sounded like a judge or a prosecutor.
-Yeah.

713
00:48:35,892 --> 00:48:37,144
That's what I'm saying.

714
00:48:37,227 --> 00:48:40,147
I don't know how,
but the words just flew out of my mouth.

715
00:48:40,647 --> 00:48:44,026
Before I lost my memory,
maybe I was a pro…

716
00:48:48,572 --> 00:48:50,365
-A pro…
-A pro what?

717
00:48:52,784 --> 00:48:53,744
A pro…

718
00:48:54,828 --> 00:48:56,705
A prodigy!

719
00:48:56,788 --> 00:48:58,498
-You were amazing.
-You're smart.

720
00:48:58,582 --> 00:48:59,875
You're amazing.

721
00:49:00,625 --> 00:49:01,501
Or properly scary.

722
00:49:01,585 --> 00:49:03,211
-Surprising, yeah?
-She's smart.

723
00:49:05,047 --> 00:49:07,007
I want the rematch today.

724
00:49:07,090 --> 00:49:08,091
You…

725
00:49:08,175 --> 00:49:09,968
-You're in no state to--
-I can do it.

726
00:49:10,052 --> 00:49:12,721
I don't want a silver medal.
I'll do the rematch today.

727
00:49:15,223 --> 00:49:16,391
Please let him do that.

728
00:49:17,184 --> 00:49:20,145
The bleeding has almost stopped,
and an athlete knows his body best.

729
00:49:20,228 --> 00:49:23,815
The flow of the match was good today,
so Pil-seung must have a good feeling.

730
00:49:30,781 --> 00:49:33,867
BOXING ASSOCIATION OF KOREA
NO ENTRY

731
00:49:37,037 --> 00:49:38,789
Hey!

732
00:49:41,625 --> 00:49:43,585
We told you to go back for now.

733
00:49:43,668 --> 00:49:45,670
The referees and officials
are discussing it,

734
00:49:45,754 --> 00:49:48,381
so if you wait in the waiting room,
we'll let you know.

735
00:49:50,092 --> 00:49:51,343
Hey!

736
00:49:51,426 --> 00:49:56,264
I won't put a silver medal
around my boy's neck like this!

737
00:49:56,765 --> 00:49:59,476
Even if he gets a silver medal,

738
00:49:59,976 --> 00:50:02,312
it happens today, you hear?

739
00:50:02,813 --> 00:50:03,647
Please!

740
00:50:03,730 --> 00:50:07,484
Let him fight today in his gloves
for whatever medal!

741
00:50:08,151 --> 00:50:09,319
Okay?

742
00:50:09,402 --> 00:50:11,113
Are you listening?

743
00:50:13,406 --> 00:50:14,449
You hear?

744
00:50:20,330 --> 00:50:21,164
How did it go?

745
00:50:23,708 --> 00:50:24,543
Have a seat.

746
00:50:33,552 --> 00:50:34,386
Are you sure

747
00:50:35,595 --> 00:50:36,680
you're up for it?

748
00:50:40,934 --> 00:50:41,768
Okay.

749
00:50:42,519 --> 00:50:43,478
Pil-seung.

750
00:50:44,396 --> 00:50:45,230
It's okay to lose.

751
00:50:47,107 --> 00:50:51,069
For not giving up
and keeping your gloves on until the end,

752
00:50:51,153 --> 00:50:53,613
you've already won gold in my eyes.

753
00:51:04,583 --> 00:51:06,209
I have a favor to ask.

754
00:51:08,044 --> 00:51:09,462
Just don't get hurt.

755
00:51:18,722 --> 00:51:20,765
FINAL
KIM PIL-SEUNG VS CHOI WON-UK

756
00:51:22,434 --> 00:51:23,435
Please.

757
00:51:23,518 --> 00:51:26,021
-Pil-seung.
-Pil-seung, you've got this!

758
00:51:30,400 --> 00:51:31,443
Come on, Pil-seung!

759
00:51:31,526 --> 00:51:32,360
Go, taffy fists!

760
00:51:36,740 --> 00:51:37,949
That's it.

761
00:51:38,909 --> 00:51:40,076
Yeah, that's it.

762
00:51:40,160 --> 00:51:42,495
-Circle more.
-Keep moving!

763
00:51:43,288 --> 00:51:44,331
Get closer!

764
00:51:48,668 --> 00:51:49,961
-Oh my!
-Do it!

765
00:51:50,045 --> 00:51:52,422
-Stay on him! Corner him!
-Lead hand.

766
00:51:57,260 --> 00:51:59,304
-Oh no!
-Guard up.

767
00:52:06,811 --> 00:52:08,230
Red, back to your corner.

768
00:52:23,703 --> 00:52:25,163
Red corner wins by KO!

769
00:52:27,791 --> 00:52:29,251
Pil-seung, good job!

770
00:52:29,334 --> 00:52:31,253
Great job, Pil-seung!

771
00:52:31,336 --> 00:52:32,462
Come here.

772
00:52:32,545 --> 00:52:33,880
Good job!

773
00:52:34,381 --> 00:52:36,258
Pil-seung, you did great!

774
00:52:49,479 --> 00:52:51,106
You did well. You were great.

775
00:52:51,606 --> 00:52:52,649
You did great.

776
00:52:53,275 --> 00:52:55,819
Great work. Congratulations on gold.

777
00:52:55,902 --> 00:52:56,987
Coach!

778
00:53:00,490 --> 00:53:01,950
Wait one second.

779
00:53:26,349 --> 00:53:28,935
Why are you crying? I won.

780
00:53:33,773 --> 00:53:35,942
This is why!

781
00:53:36,026 --> 00:53:40,697
This is why I didn't want you to fight.

782
00:53:41,531 --> 00:53:47,662
Goodness, just look at your face.

783
00:53:48,955 --> 00:53:51,791
Did you really have to go
all the way to the end?

784
00:53:52,667 --> 00:53:54,627
You could have waited
until you were better.

785
00:53:55,253 --> 00:53:57,630
Did you really
have to go as far as to draw blood?

786
00:53:59,174 --> 00:54:00,258
Because of you, Mom.

787
00:54:02,093 --> 00:54:05,430
If I had a rematch on another day,
you'd have to cry again.

788
00:54:06,431 --> 00:54:07,807
Red corner wins by KO!

789
00:54:08,308 --> 00:54:10,352
Advancing to the final, red corner.

790
00:54:17,859 --> 00:54:19,736
Red corner wins by KO!

791
00:54:24,574 --> 00:54:26,743
Seeing you there gave me strength.

792
00:54:26,826 --> 00:54:28,745
That's why I won.

793
00:54:31,122 --> 00:54:32,332
Thanks for coming, Mom.

794
00:54:37,295 --> 00:54:38,296
You rascal.

795
00:54:39,339 --> 00:54:40,757
You rascal!

796
00:54:40,840 --> 00:54:43,385
You damn rascal!

797
00:54:44,344 --> 00:54:48,056
Why did I even give birth to you?

798
00:54:48,640 --> 00:54:49,766
Okay.

799
00:54:50,975 --> 00:54:52,102
It's okay, Mom.

800
00:54:54,813 --> 00:54:56,272
Why did you give birth to me?

801
00:54:56,856 --> 00:54:59,275
So you could see me
win a gold medal, of course.

802
00:55:03,822 --> 00:55:05,657
Good job, my baby.

803
00:55:05,740 --> 00:55:07,367
I'm so proud of you, my son.

804
00:55:08,868 --> 00:55:09,953
I didn't even know

805
00:55:11,371 --> 00:55:14,082
my Pil-seung was this amazing.

806
00:55:15,417 --> 00:55:18,837
I'm sorry I didn't know.

807
00:55:22,424 --> 00:55:23,425
It's okay.

808
00:55:40,483 --> 00:55:41,526
You're crying again?

809
00:55:42,944 --> 00:55:45,655
Young man, maybe you should get checked
for menopause?

810
00:55:50,034 --> 00:55:51,953
I'm in my twenties.

811
00:55:54,581 --> 00:55:55,415
What?

812
00:55:57,792 --> 00:56:00,003
-He said he's in his twenties.
-Tae-ha.

813
00:56:04,382 --> 00:56:06,259
-This is perfectly fine.
-Still, stop it.

814
00:56:06,342 --> 00:56:07,719
It'll hurt.

815
00:56:07,802 --> 00:56:10,430
It doesn't hurt. I'm a gold medalist.

816
00:56:16,519 --> 00:56:19,689
-Are we having a feast at Pil-seung's?
-Barbecue?

817
00:56:19,772 --> 00:56:21,024
-Damn right.
-Yeah, let's.

818
00:56:21,107 --> 00:56:22,901
-Hui-ja's treat.
-What are we eating?

819
00:56:22,984 --> 00:56:24,277
Let's just eat at home.

820
00:56:24,360 --> 00:56:26,154
Let's have some barbecue…

821
00:56:26,654 --> 00:56:28,198
They look great.

822
00:56:28,698 --> 00:56:34,329
It feels like I'm watching
a TV show's happy ending.

823
00:56:35,371 --> 00:56:38,500
Wasn't I also like a character
in a TV show today?

824
00:56:39,459 --> 00:56:42,504
Wasn't I sort of awesome earlier?

825
00:56:43,505 --> 00:56:46,758
Where did that come from earlier?
Did you remember something?

826
00:56:49,219 --> 00:56:51,971
I don't really know
where it came from either.

827
00:56:53,139 --> 00:56:57,352
It does sort of feel like
I've done that before.

828
00:56:57,852 --> 00:57:01,689
If I'm honest, I've felt kind of weird
since I got here today.

829
00:57:02,524 --> 00:57:05,109
I feel like I've been here before.

830
00:57:06,361 --> 00:57:09,322
Is this the only boxing arena?

831
00:57:10,073 --> 00:57:11,157
No.

832
00:57:12,325 --> 00:57:14,702
But I like this one the most.

833
00:57:15,662 --> 00:57:16,496
Why?

834
00:57:17,205 --> 00:57:18,456
I met my first love here.

835
00:57:21,501 --> 00:57:24,963
That darn first love of yours
is really getting on my nerves.

836
00:57:29,133 --> 00:57:31,678
It was nice meeting you,
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.

837
00:57:39,185 --> 00:57:41,062
What was his name again?

838
00:57:45,775 --> 00:57:47,402
I want to remember it.

839
00:57:52,615 --> 00:57:54,617
What? Did you remember something else?

840
00:57:55,868 --> 00:57:56,995
Yes.

841
00:57:57,078 --> 00:58:00,540
I think I met some guy here
a long time ago.

842
00:58:03,835 --> 00:58:05,211
Do you remember anything else?

843
00:58:10,758 --> 00:58:11,593
No.

844
00:58:12,260 --> 00:58:14,596
I don't remember any details,

845
00:58:14,679 --> 00:58:18,308
but I think that guy was really

846
00:58:18,391 --> 00:58:20,560
handsome.

847
00:58:21,686 --> 00:58:25,023
-What?
-He had a really good vibe, and…

848
00:58:25,607 --> 00:58:26,441
Right!

849
00:58:26,524 --> 00:58:29,235
He said he was a future gold medalist.

850
00:58:29,861 --> 00:58:30,903
Yeah.

851
00:58:30,987 --> 00:58:34,282
And judging by
how I kept glancing back wistfully,

852
00:58:34,365 --> 00:58:37,535
I think I must have liked that guy a lot.

853
00:58:38,161 --> 00:58:39,287
He was handsome.

854
00:58:43,249 --> 00:58:45,918
That's why you should stop
talking about your first love.

855
00:58:46,002 --> 00:58:49,839
I just don't remember him now,
but I had a guy like that too.

856
00:59:00,558 --> 00:59:01,392
Wait for me.

857
00:59:18,951 --> 00:59:21,913
Jang Tae-ha,
I'm off to work at the taffy workshop.

858
01:00:27,562 --> 01:00:28,980
Is this yours, sir?

859
01:00:50,918 --> 01:00:52,587
OUR STICKY LOVE

860
01:01:39,217 --> 01:01:43,179
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

